{"assets":["/statement-assets/90d4996e4a98415630168abb4482b063a3c91acb2ee0dc57927adedcfe1d8a81.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1823","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Removing Graph"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob are playing a game on a graph. They have an undirected graph without self-loops and multiple edges. All vertices of the graph have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"degree equal to $$$2$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The graph may consist of several components. Note that if such graph has $$$n$$$ vertices, it will have exactly $$$n$$$ edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob take turn. Alice goes first. In each turn, the player can choose $$$k$$$ ($$$l \\le k \\le r$$$; $$$l \\lt r$$$) vertices that form "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a connected subgraph"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and erase these vertices from the graph, including all incident edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The player who can't make a step loses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, suppose they are playing on the given graph with given $$$l = 2$$$ and $$$r = 3$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/90d4996e4a98415630168abb4482b063a3c91acb2ee0dc57927adedcfe1d8a81.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A valid vertex set for Alice to choose at the first move is one of the following: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 2\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{2, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{4, 5\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{4, 6\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{5, 6\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{4, 5, 6\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Suppose, Alice chooses subgraph $$$\\{4, 6\\}$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then a valid vertex set for Bob to choose at the first move is one of the following: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 2\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{2, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Suppose, Bob chooses subgraph $$$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice can't make a move, so she loses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a graph of size $$$n$$$ and integers $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$. Who will win if both Alice and Bob play optimally."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\le l \\lt r \\le n$$$) — the number of vertices in the graph, and the constraints on the number of vertices Alice or Bob can choose in one move."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next $$$n$$$ lines contains edges of the graph: one edge per line. The $$$i$$$-th line contains two integers $$$u_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le n$$$; $$$u_i \\neq v_i$$$) — description of the $$$i$$$-th edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the degree of each vertex of the given graph is equal to $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (case-insensitive) if Alice wins, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 2 3\n1 2\n2 3\n3 1\n4 5\n5 6\n6 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nBob\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 1 2\n1 2\n2 3\n3 1\n4 5\n5 6\n6 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nBob\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n12 1 3\n1 2\n2 3\n3 1\n4 5\n5 6\n6 7\n7 4\n8 9\n9 10\n10 11\n11 12\n12 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nAlice\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test the same input as in legend is shown."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test the same graph as in legend is shown, but with $$$l = 1$$$ and $$$r = 2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1823E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1823/problem/E"}